{"book":24,"chapter":26,"context":{"chapter":26,"title":"Jeremiah on Trial","summary":"When Jeremiah warns that the temple will become like Shiloh, priests and prophets demand his death, but officials and elders defend him by recalling how Hezekiah heeded the prophet Micah. Another prophet, Urijah, is executed, while Ahikam protects Jeremiah.","background":"This chapter tells how people reacted to the sermon of chapter 7. The elders quote Micah 3:12 word for word, about a century after Micah spoke it. Ahikam son of Shaphan belonged to a family of royal officials who supported Jeremiah; his son Gedaliah later became governor (40:5).","customs":[{"term":"The graves of the common people","verses":"26:23","note":"A public burial ground in the Kidron Valley (2 Kings 23:6). Denying Urijah a family tomb was a final disgrace."}],"watchFor":["'Diminish not a word' (v. 2).","The shape of a trial: charge (v. 11), defense (vv. 12–15), verdict (v. 16), precedent (vv. 17–19).","Urijah's fate shows how real the danger was (vv. 20–23)."],"connections":["Micah 3:12","Jeremiah 7:12-14","2 Kings 22:12","Acts 5:38-39"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["בְּרֵאשִׁית","bereshit","H7225","HR/Ncfsc","in [the] beginning of"],["מַמְלְכוּת","mamlekhut","H4468","HNcfsc","[the] reign of"],["יְהוֹיָקִים","yehoyakim","H3079","HNpm","Jehoiakim"],["בֶּן","ben-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["יֹאשִׁיָּהוּ","yoshiyahu","H2977","HNpm","Josiah"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh","H4428","HNcmsc","[the] king of"],["יְהוּדָה","yehudah","H3063","HNpl","Judah"],["הָיָה","hayah","H1961","HVqp3ms","it came"],["הַדָּבָר","hadavar","H1697","HTd/Ncmsa","the word"],["הַזֶּה","hazeh","H2088","HTd/Tm","<the> this"],["מֵאֵת","me'et","H854","HR/R","from with"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"]],"x":[[14036004,14036005,4],[24027001,24027001,3]],"xn":2},"2":{"w":[["כֹּה","koh","H3541","HD","thus"],["אָמַר","'amar","H559","HVqp3ms","he said"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahwe